When verifying programs that use output like `printf,puts,fprintf`, Symbiotic is unable to tell the difference between output from klee and output from the verified program. 

To reproduce the problem, verify memcleanup of the following program with `--no-slice`:

```c
extern int printf(const char *, ...);

int main()
{
    printf("KLEE: ERROR: malicious.c:5: memory error: memory not cleaned up");
    return 0;
}
```

Fortunately, error replay prevents us from producing incorrect answer, but this prevents Symbiotic from answering correctly. I suggest we somehow ignore calls of these functions in klee.

Looks like sv-comp will include benchmarks using `atexit` function in MemSafety category. 

I tested Symbiotic 3ea77c5 on the testing program below (after preprocessing) and it produces incorrect result. This is the command I used to run Symbiotic: `./symbiotic --sv-comp --prp memcleanup test_atexit.i`. I tried even with `--no-slice` and the problem persists. I expect Symbiotic to report `true`, but it reports `false`. Symbiotic probably doesn't understand atexit even though klee has some support for it.

```c
#include <stdlib.h>

static int *p;

void free_glob(void) {
    free(p);
}

int main() {
    p = (int*) malloc(sizeof(int));
    atexit(free_glob);
    return 0;
}
```
